  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Niassa Integrated HIV and AIDS Programme - Progresso</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progresso&#x2019;s project is part of a wider programme in Niassa Province, the Niassa Integrated HIV&amp;AIDS Programme. The project aims to create awareness and improve the knowledge of the communities about the HIV/AIDS pandemic as well as to mitigate its impact through food security and nutrition interventions. The project expects to bring improvements in the nutritional status of the PLWHIV, Orphaned and Vulnerable Children (OVC) and to the wider community; it also envisages to contribute to the reduction of the level of new infections of HIV amongst the youth and women as well as to open opportunities for education of OVC. It will also intend to empower local organizations, particularly the community based organisations (CBO&#x2019;s) concerned with the HIV&amp;AIDS pandemic.

The project&#x2019;s main strategies will be on capacity building of local/traditional leaders (including initiation rites masters), on issues related with HIV prevention; use of communication strategies for information dissemination such as theatre, media material, etc; most of which in local language.  Other target groups will be involved will be the associations of PLWHVA kindergartens, vocational centre, etc.</narrative>
  </description>
